.Dd July 8, 2026
.Dt NEW_FOUNDATION 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm new_foundation
.Nd build and archive a FreeBSD foundation from source
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl s Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar key=value
.Op Fl q
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility builds a FreeBSD world and kernel from source and archives the
result as a
.Em foundation .
A foundation is a pristine base build from which systems and containers
branch.
.Pp
Build configuration is stored in
.Pa recipes/foundations/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /build.conf
and can be supplied interactively, via
.Fl o
overrides, or through defaults in
.Pa parasa.conf .
.Pp
.Nm
operates in three modes:
.Bl -tag -width "Semi-interactive"
.It Em Interactive
When
.Fl s
is not given, the user is prompted for all configuration values.
.It Em Semi-interactive
When
.Fl s
is given without
.Fl q ,
the user is prompted for configuration values, with any
.Fl o
overrides offered as defaults.
.It Em Quiet
When both
.Fl s
and
.Fl q
are given, no prompts are issued.
Specifying
.Fl q
twice additionally suppresses progress output.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-o key=value"
.It Fl h
Display usage information and exit.
.It Fl d
Dry run.
Show what would be done without making changes.
.It Fl s Ar name
Set the foundation name.
Required when running in quiet mode.
.It Fl o Ar key=value
Override a build configuration key.
May be specified multiple times.
Recognized keys:
.Bl -tag -width "src_branch" -compact
.It Cm src_branch
Source branch to build from.
Default:
.Li stable/15 .
.It Cm kernconf
Kernel configuration file.
Default:
.Li GENERIC .
.It Cm make_jobs
Number of parallel make jobs.
Default: value of
.Va hw.ncpu .
.El
.It Fl q
Quiet mode.
Suppress interactive prompts; requires
.Fl s .
When specified twice
.Pq Fl qq ,
progress output is also suppressed.
.El
.Sh EXECUTION FLOW
.Nm
proceeds through the following stages:
.Bl -enum
.It
Collect the foundation name and build configuration.
.It
Create
.Pa recipes/foundations/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /build.conf .
.It
Ensure the FreeBSD source tree is present at
.Pa zshemot/torah .
.It
Create a transient workspace at
.Pa zshemot/tablets .
.It
Execute the five make targets:
.Cm buildworld ,
.Cm buildkernel ,
.Cm installkernel ,
.Cm installworld ,
and
.Cm distribution .
.It
Commit the result to a
.Li foundation/ Ns Ar name
orphan branch on
.Pa zbamidbar/sinai.git .
.It
Create a ZFS snapshot and archive to
.Pa zbamidbar/sinai.zfs/foundations/ Ns Ar name .
.It
Destroy the transient workspace.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "recipes/foundations/<name>/build.conf"
.It Pa recipes/foundations/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /build.conf
Per-foundation build configuration produced by
.Nm .
Contains
.Va SRC_BRANCH ,
.Va KERNCONF ,
and
.Va MAKE_JOBS .
.It Pa parasa.conf
Framework-wide configuration providing fallback defaults.
.It Pa etc/mtree.ignore
List of paths excluded from mtree comparison.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build a foundation interactively:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_foundation
.Ed
.Pp
Build a foundation with a custom kernel configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_foundation -s mybase -o kernconf=MYKERNEL
.Ed
.Pp
Fully automated build with no prompts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_foundation -s prod15 -o src_branch=stable/15 -q
.Ed
.Pp
Preview what a quiet build would do:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# new_foundation -s prod15 -d -q
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr new_system 8 ,
.Xr new_container 8 ,
.Xr deploy_system 8
